From: BPI-W2 PiKVM <jalen.lin@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msd: nbd: keep the image while the remote is offline

Since 4.221 (c4582da7, "drop image if both kvmd and kvmd-nbd were
restarted") the drive is ejected on every change KVMD-NBD reports while a
remote image is attached: the drive's file is then always the NBD device,
last_known_path. That includes the remote going offline for a moment, which
4.219 rode out. The eject is a write to the gadget's forced_eject from the
event loop. When the host is in the middle of a read from the NBD device,
f_mass_storage holds the LUN's lock in that read, which waits for the
remote, so the write blocks and kvmd stops answering altogether (Web UI,
API, HID) until the remote is back.

Eject when the binding behind the drive is gone or no longer running, or
when KVMD-NBD itself is unreachable, as 4.219 did; the restart case the
change was for is still covered (the restarted KVMD-NBD has no running
binding).

Checked on a BPI-W2: with the server stopped during a read, kvmd kept
answering and the image stayed attached; once the server was back the
target read it again. Restarting kvmd-nbd, or kvmd-nbd and kvmd, still
ejected it.
---
diff --git a/kvmd/plugins/msd/otg/__init__.py b/kvmd/plugins/msd/otg/__init__.py
index 4c1eb474..02fc9a3f 100644
--- a/kvmd/plugins/msd/otg/__init__.py
+++ b/kvmd/plugins/msd/otg/__init__.py
@@ -555,13 +555,13 @@ class Plugin(BaseMsd):  # pylint: disable=too-many-instance-attributes
             try:
                 try:
                     async for _ in self.__nbd.poll_for_changes():
-                        self.__poke_drive_for_nbd()
+                        self.__poke_drive_for_nbd(False)
                         if not ok:
                             logger.info("NBD online")
                             ok = True
                 except Exception:
                     if ok:
-                        self.__poke_drive_for_nbd()
+                        self.__poke_drive_for_nbd(True)
                     raise
             except Exception as ex:
                 if ok:
@@ -572,9 +572,14 @@ class Plugin(BaseMsd):  # pylint: disable=too-many-instance-attributes
                     ok = False
                 await asyncio.sleep(1)
 
-    def __poke_drive_for_nbd(self) -> None:
+    def __poke_drive_for_nbd(self, nbd_lost: bool) -> None:
+        # Eject only when the binding behind the drive is gone or stopped, or
+        # KVMD-NBD itself is: a change of the remote's online state alone
+        # must keep the image, or a short outage would take it from the host.
+        bound = (self.__drive.get_image_path() == self.__nbd.last_known_path)
+        running = bool(self.__nbd.image and self.__nbd.asserted_running)
         if (
-            self.__drive.get_image_path() == self.__nbd.last_known_path
+            (bound and (nbd_lost or not running))
             or (self.__nbd.image and not self.__nbd.asserted_running)
         ):
             self.__drive.set_image_path("")
